  "facts": [
    "Montlake Bridge, completed in 1925, was the last of Seattle’s original bascule drawbridges, boasting the highest clearance—48 feet—among the four, and uniquely featuring trunnion supports to dodge a patent lawsuit.",
    "Designed in Collegiate Gothic style by Edgar Blair, Harlan Thomas, and A.H. Albertson, the bridge’s control towers echo the University of Washington’s campus architecture, a deliberate nod by architect Carl F. Gould.",
    "From 1940 to 1970 and again after 1981, Montlake Bridge carried Seattle’s trolleybuses, making it one of only two movable bridges in the Western Hemisphere still traversed by electric streetcars."
